   149	"Only yours." Dace rubbed out a dot beside another name and wrote it in somewhere else, as though the two things had nothing to do with each other. "He's been watching you, and he hasn't been watching anybody else, and he sat very still in the fifth exchange of your Ulric bout, and didn't cheer, and didn't groan, and went home." Dace turned his head and looked at Cael properly. "I don't have to put you on with him. There's a Shield from Fenrow who'd take the slot and fall over for the money. But I thought you'd rather know who's sitting in that seat than not."
